### ImageMagick version

7.1.0

### Operating system

Linux

### Operating system, version and so on

Ubuntu 22.04

### Description

Trying the test case with dissolve on line 119: 

https://github.com/ImageMagick/ImageMagick/blob/25e3a4f3845f59536d19aba0ac0580aa6715147f/PerlMagick/demo/compose-specials.pl#L119

the destination disappears completely for all values of `args` that I have tested: Example for args = 50:

![test](https://github.com/ImageMagick/ImageMagick/assets/6708379/e0e50a1c-6beb-4a35-a97c-cef91b356545)

Here is the code I am using:

```perl
use strict;
use warnings;
use feature qw(say);
use Image::Magick;

my $dest=Image::Magick->new();
$dest->Read('logo:');
$dest->Crop('100x100+400+100');  # wizards hat
$dest->Set(page=>'0x0+0+0');
$dest->Set(alpha=>'Set');

# Source, Composite or Overlay image
my $src=Image::Magick->new();
$src->Set(size=>'80x80');
$src->Read('gradient:black-white');
$src->Set(alpha=>'Set');

my $offset="+10+10";

$dest->Composite(
  image=>$src,
  compose=>'dissolve',
  args=>'50',
  geometry=>$offset,
);

{
    my $error = $dest->Write( 'test.jpg' );
    die "Cannot write new.jpg: $error" if $error;
}
```

Expected output would be somthing like:

![test](https://github.com/ImageMagick/ImageMagick/assets/6708379/e1a526eb-371c-41ca-a19b-3778c5679561)


### Steps to Reproduce

Run the shown perl code (perl 5.36) to reproduce.

